    "incidents:pm-2047_withdrawals_postmortem.md"
   ],
   "answer": "The payment-processing delays in March 2026 were triggered by three low-risk system changes:\n1. **CHG-1042** - reduced the PayFlex connection-pool maximum size in **payment-gateway** from 200 to 50 (deployed 2026-03-09). This caused connection-pool exhaustion and deposit-request time-outs.\n2. **CHG-1051** - released fraud-scoring model v3.2 (deployed 2026-03-12 09:15 UTC). The new model responded slowly (p99 \u2248 450 ms vs 80 ms) and contributed to the deposit delay.\n3. **CHG-1047** - introduced a new index idx_entries_account_created on the **ledger_entries** table (migration started 2026-03-18 22:00 UTC). The migration blocked ledger writes, stalling withdrawals.\n\n**Affected services**\n- For the deposit-delay incident (INC-2041): **payment-gateway**, **fraud-scoring**, and **wallet-service** experienced delays; **ledger-service** and withdrawals were not affected\u3010S1\u3011.\n- For the withdrawal-stall incident (INC-2047): **ledger-service**, **wallet-service**, and **payment-gateway** (payouts) were impacted\u3010S4\u3011.\n\n**Documents confirming these facts**\n- Postmortem PM-2041 (final) - details the root cause (CHG-1042, CHG-1051) and lists the affected services\u3010S1\u3011.\n- Draft postmortem PM-2041 (v0.9) - repeats the same root-cause changes and service impact\u3010S2\u3011.\n- Q1 2026 reliability review - summarises that the March deposit delay (INC-2041) was caused by CHG-1042 and CHG-1051\u3010S3\u3011.\n- Incident report INC-2047 - describes the withdrawal stall caused by CHG-1047 and the services affected\u3010S4\u3011.\n",
